# Kyosei store link, written by `kyo init` (KYO-54/KYO-56).
#
# This project's store -- its records, its ideas/ intake layer, its shift notes,
# its evidence artifacts and the frozen briefs quoting all of them -- lives
# OUTSIDE this repository, at the path below, committed to its own git repository
# there. This one-line pointer is the only thing about the store that is
# committed here.
#
# store: read by kyosei.config.resolve_layout, which is how every `kyo` command
# finds this project. A path starting with ~ resolves against the current user's
# home directory (so this file survives being cloned onto another machine); a
# relative path resolves against this file's own directory.
store: ~/kyosei/recx
